---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="legal prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <address>
      Marc Borer<br />
      Hirzengarten 2<br />
      4226 Breitenbach<br />
      Schweiz
    </address>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:mb@marc-borer.ch">mb@marc-borer.ch</a></p>

    <h2>2. General</h2>
    <p>
      Protecting your personal data is important to us. This privacy policy informs you
      about the collection and processing of personal data when using this website in
      accordance with the Swiss Data Protection Act (nDSG) and, where applicable, the
      European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>, a service provided by
      Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Cloudflare runs a
      global network; requests from Switzerland and the EU are usually answered by data
      centres in Europe.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you access this website, the following data is automatically collected in
      server logs and processed by Cloudflare:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>Date and time of the request</li>
      <li>Requested page (URL)</li>
      <li>Referrer URL</li>
      <li>Browser type and version (User-Agent)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cloudflare processes this data to operate and secure the service, in particular to
      fend off attacks. For more information, see the
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Web Analytics with Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      To measure reach, this website uses <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, a service
      provided by Cloudflare, Inc. It works without cookies and without storing personal
      data: no visitor profiles are built, no cross-device identifiers are created, and no
      data about visitors is passed to third parties. It records aggregate values such as page
      views, the referring page, country, browser and device type, and load times (Core Web
      Vitals).
    </p>
    <p>
      Because no personal data is stored and no cookies are set, this measurement needs no
      consent. For more information, see
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>
      and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
    <p>This website sets no cookies. The only entry stored in your browser's local storage is:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>theme</code> — your preferred colour scheme (light/dark), only once you use the toggle</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This entry never leaves your browser and can be deleted at any time in your browser settings.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Transfer to the USA</h2>
    <p>
      Hosting and web analytics at Cloudflare may transfer data to the USA. The USA currently
      has an adequacy decision under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (DPF) and the
      Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. Cloudflare, Inc. is certified under the DPF.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the Swiss Data Protection Act (nDSG) and, where applicable, the GDPR, you
      have the following rights:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right of access</strong> — You may request information about your stored personal data</li>
      <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — You may request the correction of inaccurate data</li>
      <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — You may request the deletion of your data</li>
      <li><strong>Right to restriction</strong> — You may request the restriction of data processing</li>
      <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — You may receive your data in a common format</li>
      <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — You may object to the processing of your data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise your rights, please contact:
      <a href="mailto:mb@marc-borer.ch">mb@marc-borer.ch</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe that the processing of your data violates data protection law, you
      may file a complaint with the Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner
      (FDPIC): <a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.edoeb.admin.ch</a>
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This privacy policy may be updated at any time. The current version is available
      on this page.
    </p>
    <p class="legal-date">Last updated: April 2026</p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 46rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--space-8);
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal address {
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
